  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If object properties can be extended with RELS-EXT (both relationship properties and descriptive",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "properties), then it would be good to allow XACML policies to be written that refer to these properties",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "in the Resource target specification of the policy.  This can be done by modifying the DOReader to include",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "RELS-EXT properties along with core properties. The XACML attribute finder code uses DOReader to get object attributes, so it can take whatever it gets from DOReader.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
